  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: B4a: gitutil.execute_outcome, head_sha, _git_in timeout and a pure porcelain parser shared by test with daemon._dirty_scope_paths",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, SPLIT after three spec-review rounds (T-1435, T-1453, T-1468). The commit-now resume of T-1435 stays DROPPED (no non_json case has a session).\n\nContract (plan.md): gitutil.execute_outcome(worktree, parent, scope, *, since=None) -> {ahead, head,\ndirty_in_scope, dirty_out_of_scope} | None; hold prefix 'execute_incomplete' (B5 maps it to failure kind\n'incomplete').\n\nEvidence (U2, 2026-10-01): status_reason non_json is set in spawn.run_worker when json.loads of the\n`claude -p --output-format json` stdout fails; every recorded case is 'non-JSON output (rc=143): ' with empty\noutput (SIGTERM). luna T-0526: the worker posted done itself through bus_post_result with a prose summary and\nreconcile marked the process dead. So the signal is the git state of the worktree, and a result the worker\nalready posted must win.\n\nFacts (goal/T-1403; spawn.py/gitutil.py/worker_control.py unchanged since main 355583c):\n- spawn.run_worker sets t['executor'] = 'claude:<tier>' for execute before run_claude; the done path posts\n  {'summary', 'executed_by': f\"claude:{tier}\", 'review'} with no commit; the failed path posts status failed,\n  reason, resume_hint.partial_output. Every write goes through worker_control.write_if_current (bus lock +\n  is_current(epoch)). run_claude returns only after the child process has exited (waits on the Popen); the\n  reaper path (worker_control) can mark the epoch stale while the child is still alive.\n- gitutil._git_in(worktree, *args) has no timeout; _resolve_base(worktree, parent); callers reconcile_dead and\n  changed_paths must keep their behaviour.\n- daemon._dirty_scope_paths parses `git status --porcelain -z --untracked-files=all` (rename pairs, ignores\n  .orchestrator/ and .venv); scopes.matches(path, entries) implements the same matching. Do not import daemon\n  from gitutil.\n\nChange (pure, read-only git evidence; nothing in spawn.py changes here):\n1. gitutil._git_in(worktree, *args, timeout=None): keyword-only timeout, default None keeps every existing caller unchanged;\n   subprocess.TimeoutExpired is caught explicitly wherever a timeout is passed.\n2. gitutil.parse_porcelain_z(output: str) -> list[str]: pure parser of `git status --porcelain -z --untracked-files=all`\n   output: rename pairs yield the new path, deletions are included, .orchestrator/ and .venv prefixes are ignored. No I/O.\n3. gitutil.head_sha(worktree, timeout=60) -> sha | None.\n4. gitutil.execute_outcome(worktree, parent, scope, *, since=None) -> {'ahead', 'head', 'dirty_in_scope', 'dirty_out_of_scope'}\n   | None: None when worktree is not a directory, not a git work tree, no base resolves, or any git call fails (non-zero rc,\n   OSError, TimeoutExpired); every git call uses timeout=60. ahead = rev-list --count <since or base>..HEAD; dirty paths from\n   parse_porcelain_z; in/out by scopes.matches(path, scope). Read-only.\nParity: tests/test_gitutil.py feeds one identical porcelain -z sample (rename pair, deletion, untracked file, .orchestrator/\nand .venv entries) to gitutil.parse_porcelain_z and to daemon._dirty_scope_paths (test-only import of daemon; gitutil never\nimports daemon) and asserts the same path set.\nRollback: `git revert` of the merge; no caller depends on the new functions until B4b lands.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests. Locate every insertion point by symbol, never by line number.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1490"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_execute_outcome_reports_ahead_head_and_dirty_split_by_scope: passes: in a scratch repo with a goal branch and a task worktree, gitutil.execute_outcome(worktree, parent, scope) returns ahead (commits since merge-base with goal/<parent>), head sha, and uncommitted paths split into dirty_in_scope / dirty_out_of_scope (untracked and deleted paths included, .orchestrator/ and .venv ignored, scopes.matches rules); with since=<sha of an older commit> ahead counts only commits after it; returns None for a directory that is not a git work tree, when a git call fails, and when a git call raises subprocess.TimeoutExpired (patched); existing _git_in callers pass no timeout and behave as before",
    "tests/test_gitutil.py::test_parse_porcelain_z_matches_daemon_dirty_scope_paths: passes: the same porcelain -z sample (rename pair, deletion, untracked, .orchestrator/ and .venv entries) gives the same path set from gitutil.parse_porcelain_z and daemon._dirty_scope_paths, and gitutil does not import daemon",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/gitutil.py",
    "tests/test_gitutil.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
