    {
      "ts": 1790893586.4244769,
      "status": "done",
      "result": {
        "summary": "The implementation matches the contract. The tests are weaker than the acceptance criteria require, and the parity check passes only because of the sample's scope. I read the diff and the code it depends on but did not run the tests.",
        "verdict": "request_changes",
        "comments": [
          {
            "path": "tests/test_gitutil.py",
            "line": 29,
            "issue": "The since=<older sha> check cannot fail. older is HEAD~1, which is also the merge-base with goal/P, so ahead is 1 with or without `since`. The test needs a repo with at least two commits after the base, then a `since` that gives a different count (for example 2 without it, 1 with it). As written, a bug that ignores `since` would still pass.",
            "severity": "med"
          },
          {
            "path": "tests/test_gitutil.py",
            "line": 34,
            "issue": "Acceptance requires None for a directory that is not a git work tree and None when a git call fails (non-zero rc). The test covers only a nonexistent path and a patched TimeoutExpired. It has no case for an existing non-git directory (a tempdir outside any repo) and none for a non-zero return code, for example a patched _git_in returning returncode=1.",
            "severity": "med"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/gitutil.py",
            "line": 13,
            "issue": "parse_porcelain_z drops the rename/copy source path, but daemon._dirty_scope_paths includes both destination and source when they are in scope. The parity test passes only because its scope omits `old/name.txt`. Scopes that include the old path would give different results, so parity is not shown. The spec says rename pairs yield the new path, so this may be intended, but the divergence should be documented and tested, or the test scope should include the source path.",
            "severity": "med"
          },
          {
            "path": "orchestrator/gitutil.py",
            "line": 38,
            "issue": "The merge-base candidate loop duplicates `_resolve_base` only to add timeout=60. Passing an optional timeout through `_resolve_base` would avoid two copies of the fallback order drifting apart. The `head_sha` helper is also unused by `execute_outcome`, which re-implements rev-parse. HEAD is read after the status call, so a concurrent commit could leave the ahead, dirty and head values from different moments.",
            "severity": "low"
          }
        ],
        "packet_version": "2088eb9b0039",
        "confidence": 0.0,
        "provenance": [
          "repo"
        ]
      }
